WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.367
Think of Module 10 as learning individual Pandas tools, and Module 11 as learning how to combine those tools into a

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:14.152
workflow. For example, filtering a DataFrame is useful by itself.

00:00:14.152 --> 00:00:17.212
Grouping data is useful by itself.

00:00:17.212 --> 00:00:21.197
Creating a new column is also useful by itself.

00:00:21.197 --> 00:00:26.547
But in a real project, you usually do several of these things together.

00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:34.532
You might filter out records that do not belong in the analysis, create a new variable, group the rows by region,

00:00:34.532 --> 00:00:38.505
calculate summary measures, and then sort the final report.

00:00:38.985 --> 00:00:41.587
That is the transition we are making here.

00:00:41.587 --> 00:00:50.502
We are moving from isolated commands toward a sequence of steps that has a clear analytical purpose.

00:00:50.502 --> 00:00:56.377
After this module, we will move into Module 12, Cleaning and Exploratory Data Analysis.

00:00:56.377 --> 00:01:04.697
The advanced Pandas techniques you learn here will be important there because cleaning and EDA often require several

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:08.585
connected transformations rather than one single command.
